  {
    "id" : "refactor_pipe_chain_start",
    "level" : "Info",
    "category" : "Comprehensibility",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Refactor Pipe Chain Start for Readability",
    "description" : "Encourages starting pipe chains with a raw value rather than a function call to improve readability.",
    "explanation" : "Pipes (`|>`) can become more readable by starting with a \"raw\" value.\n\nSo while this is easily comprehendable:\n\n    list\n    |> Enum.take(5)\n    |> Enum.shuffle\n    |> pick_winner()\n\nThis might be harder to read:\n\n    Enum.take(list, 5)\n    |> Enum.shuffle\n    |> pick_winner()\n\nAs always: This is just a suggestion. Check the configuration options for\ntweaking or disabling this check.",
    "enabled" : false,
    "timeToFix" : 3,
    "parameters" : [
      {
