  {
    "id" : "warning_expensive_empty_enum_check",
    "level" : "Warning",
    "category" : "Performance",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Avoid Expensive Empty Enum Checks",
    "description" : "This rule warns against checking if an enum's size is zero using Enum.count/1, which is inefficient because it counts all elements.",
    "explanation" : "Checking if the size of the enum is `0` can be very expensive, since you are\ndetermining the exact count of elements.\n\nChecking if an enum is empty should be done by using\n\n    Enum.empty?(enum)\n\nor\n\n    list == []\n\n\nFor Enum.count/2: Checking if an enum doesn't contain specific elements should\nbe done by using\n\n    not Enum.any?(enum, condition)",
    "enabled" : true,
    "timeToFix" : 5,
    "parameters" : [
    ],
    "languages" : [
    ]
  },
